      "content_html": "<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-1074274484-2.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-1074274484-2.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-1074274484-2.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-1074274484-2.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<img src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-1074274484-2.jpg\" style=\"width:100%;max-height:300px;object-fit:cover;\" />\n<figure><img alt=\"Why I Keep Traveling Solo After Being Attacked by a Man and Charged by a Bear\" src=\"https://cdn.outsideonline.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-1074274484-2.jpg?width=1200\" /></figure>\n<p>After surviving a knife assault while hiking abroad and a bear charge close to home in Montana, a veteran traveler explains how she manages risk and why she refuses to stay home.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com/adventure-travel/advice/solo-travel-safety/\">Why I Keep Traveling Solo After Being Attacked by a Man and Charged by a Bear</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.outsideonline.com\">Outside Online</a>.</p>",
